<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">21 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 21 December, from 69 to 1988.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/69">69 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,957 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Senate recognises Vespasian as emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The day after Vitellius was killed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, the Senate granted Vespasian the powers of emperor, ending the Year of the Four Emperors. His Flavian dynasty restored stability and began the Colosseum.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mayflower" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mayflower.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1620">1620 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">406 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A Mayflower party lands at Plymouth</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An exploring party from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayflower">Mayflower</a> landed at Plymouth harbour, where the Pilgrims decided to settle (11 December Old Style). Half the colonists died during the first winter.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1898">1898 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">128 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Curies identify radium</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Working in a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> shed, Marie and Pierre Curie detected a new, intensely radioactive element in pitchblende, announced days later as radium. Isolating it took Marie Curie another twelve years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1968">1968 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">58 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Apollo 8 launches for the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Frank Borman, Jim Lovell and Bill Anders lifted off on the first crewed flight to leave Earth's orbit. On Christmas Eve they orbited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a> and photographed 'Earthrise'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1988">1988 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">38 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A bomb destroys Pan Am Flight 103 over Lockerbie</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A bomb exploded aboard a Boeing 747 over Lockerbie in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, killing all 259 on board and 11 people on the ground. A Libyan intelligence officer was convicted in 2001.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li></ol>
